* From J. C. Shaw, "JOSS: Examples of the Use of an Experimental On-Line Computing Service", RAND P-3131, April 1965, page 4.
*  Integration of 1/x by Gauss two-point rule:

1.1 Type X,Y in form 1 if fp(X)=0.
1.2 Do part 2 for x=X+p·h, X+q·h.
2.1 Set y=1/x.
2.2 Set Y=Y+.5·h·y.
Form 1:
__   _._____
Set p=.5-.5/sqrt(3).
Set q=.5+.5/sqrt(3).
Set Y=0.
Set h=.1.
Do part 1 for X=1(h)10.
Type 10, log(10) in form 1.
*  Notice above that JOSS allows backspacing and strikeovers.
Type all.
Delete all.
! users 6
Type users.
